    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Discharge / charge energy ratio and RTE estimate (rolling 24 h)",
      "id": 23,
      "description": "Discharge/charge ratio: AC energy out over AC energy in over the last 24 h. It is NOT the round-trip efficiency unless the SOC is the same at both ends of the window: a net discharge of stored energy pushes it above the true RTE, a net charge below it (above 1 means the battery gave back energy stored earlier). RTE estimate: the same ratio, drawn only while the measured SOC changed by 3 points or less over the window, which bounds the stored-energy error at a few percent of a typical day's charge; the line has gaps whenever the condition fails. Standby draw is inside both. No battery capacity is assumed, so no SOC correction is attempted. Offline: battery.actual.discharge_kwh / charge_kwh over a window that starts and ends at the same SOC.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 47
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "(sum(increase(battery_optimizer_shadow_actual_battery_energy_kwh_total{direction=\"discharge\"}[1d]))) / ((sum(increase(battery_optimizer_shadow_actual_battery_energy_kwh_total{direction=\"charge\"}[1d]))) > 0)",
          "legendFormat": "Discharge / charge ratio",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
